    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "California recently passed a new law. It requires state clothing companies to help clothing be reused, repaired, and recycled. The law is the first of its kind in the United States. It aims to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the growing problem of fashion waste."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Every year, millions of tons of unwanted clothes end up in landfills across the state. Some of them get burnt. Some are given to thrift stores. When thrift stores can’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " these clothes, they’re often shipped in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bulk",
            "zh": "大批地"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to developing countries. In Ghana and Chile, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", unwanted clothes are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "piled",
            "ref": "v-pile"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " up in deserts and along rivers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The problem of clothing waste has been getting "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "trend",
            "ref": "v-trend"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of “fast fashion”. Under this trend, low-cost clothing moves quickly from design to retail stores. Such items are only "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or used a few times "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "on average",
            "ref": "v-on-average"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“We are hopeful this nation-leading law will reduce clothing waste,” said Fiona Hines. She has worked hard to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the passing of the law. “We also hope that, in the future, companies will produce "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "quality",
            "ref": "v-quality"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " clothes. We could repair and reuse them, and recycle when they reach their "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ".”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Under the new law, companies that make clothing and other textiles sold in California are required to create a(n) "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by 2026. This "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "non-profit",
            "ref": "v-non-profit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " group would set up hundreds of collection sites at thrift stores. People can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " unwanted clothes at these locations. They could also choose to mail them back. The group will take additional "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in all 58 counties across California to reclaim and recycle its products by 2030."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
